# Example integration-test environment for the cloud Neo4j graph fixtures.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.test` at the REPOSITORY ROOT (the directory that
# holds `.git`) and fill in the credentials of a DEDICATED Neo4j test instance.
# From this package directory that is four levels up:
#
#     cp .env.test.example ../../../../.env.test
#
# The fixture reads only the repository-root `.env.test`, so a copy kept next
# to this file is ignored.
#
# The test instance must be dedicated to testing: the `neo4j_driver` fixture
# runs `MATCH (n) DETACH DELETE n` before every integration test, so any other
# data on the instance would be destroyed. Never point these at the
# development / production Neo4j configured in `.env.nonprod`.
#
# `.env.test` is gitignored. These are placeholders only - do not commit real
# credentials. CI supplies the same three variables as secrets instead.
NEO4J_TEST_URI=neo4j+s://xxxxxxxx.databases.neo4j.io
NEO4J_TEST_USERNAME=replace-me
NEO4J_TEST_PASSWORD=replace-me
